{
  "rules": [
    "Apply aggressive downward correction (mean reversion) immediately following any price spike above 95 EUR, as the model consistently fails to anticipate the subsequent sharp crash (overshoot error of 20-30 EUR).",
    "Reduce forecast horizon bias: The model exhibits a persistent upward drift (lag) in the 15-30 day window; truncate long-term forecasts to the current spot price or recent 7-day average rather than projecting gradual increases.",
    "Invert sentiment weighting: Positive sentiment spikes (e.g., +0.40 to +0.60) correlate with immediate price peaks followed by rapid declines; treat positive sentiment as a contrarian sell signal rather than a bullish indicator.",
    "Adjust for volatility clustering: When history shows a rapid ascent (e.g., 80 to 98 in 10 days), reduce the forecast slope by 50% and introduce a negative drift term to account for the inevitable correction phase.",
    "Ignore sentiment neutrality during downtrends: When sentiment is 0.00 during a falling price trend, the model's assumption of stability is incorrect; force a downward adjustment based on the recent 5-day momentum."
  ]
}
